content:
@ESpacetime If you had IBD (colitis, crohns) you wouldn’t stop taking your medication just because you’re now asymptomatic. 

Doing so would cause dz exacerbation

Similarly, you wouldn’t stop taking semaglutide just bc you lost weight—obesity is a chronic disease just like IBD.

@elonmusk @teslaownersSV @chicago_glenn @ianmiles @dcherring @nichegamer Is Wegovy legit? 

I get Tony Robbins vibes from the landing page. (I came in 2nd place in an art contest for him as kid, he was using us for free marketing)

But, damn do I need to loose 30 lbs.

@AngeCrying I think I lost like 5lb/mo on wegovy lol, apparently it's normal to drop 30% of your weight in a year on it
I don't think I qualify for it anymore if I get another blood exam tho pretty sure my cholesterol fell
it's perpetually backordered and I dropped abilify anyway

@Pndulo @nunocalvin2 Ainda bem mas fez a sua parte a maioria não o faz.

researchers found that people who lost the most weight while taking semaglutide tended to then regain the most after stopping it.

https://t.co/gxXgPjP7Eo

@UnfilteredOnFox @dbongino @MartyMakary My non diabetic niece lost 150+ lbs. &amp; looks human again.  $0 w/Insurance.

There is no insulin in sema/duca glutide meds.  Wegovy (sema) is rx’ed solely for obesity.  It is the answer to obesity, a true miracle drug.  Eat healthy never hungry.

So many could live longer lives…

@seconds_0 Semaglutide et al. cause weight loss by decr. appetite (ie making you feel full faster) which sort of tracks with fiber intake apparently doing same

DPP-4 inhibitors don't primarily do this, they mostly indir. increase glucose elim. via urine

Eager to see if you get results tho

Wegovy is the first in a new generation of obesity treatments which use a hormone to regulate appetite. 

But there are side effects — and if you stop taking the drug, the weight piles back on. 

@HannahKuchler reports: https://t.co/VZIyxXtjjo

